1
00:00:01,084 --> 00:00:04,379
[STIRRING MUSIC PLAYING]

2
00:00:05,213 --> 00:00:08,174
<i>I knew it!</i>

3
00:00:08,258 --> 00:00:10,510
<i>- This is where Bea goes!</i>
<i>- Auntie?</i>

4
00:00:10,593 --> 00:00:12,011
<i>- Please, don't!</i>
<i>- Why are you here?!</i>

5
00:00:12,095 --> 00:00:13,304
<i>Mariela! Mariela.</i>

6
00:00:13,388 --> 00:00:15,265
<i>What's going on here?</i>

7
00:00:15,348 --> 00:00:16,224
<i>Ask him!</i>

8
00:00:17,434 --> 00:00:18,810
[JORDAN] <i>What are you doing here?</i>

9
00:00:18,893 --> 00:00:20,061
- [CALOY] <i>Stay back.</i>
<i>- Answer me.</i>

10
00:00:20,145 --> 00:00:21,896
<i>- Caloy!</i>
<i>- Stay back!</i>

11
00:00:21,980 --> 00:00:23,356
[PRECIOUS SCREAMS]

12
00:00:23,440 --> 00:00:24,274
<i>Caloy!</i>

13
00:00:24,357 --> 00:00:27,944
[PANTING, GRUNTING]

14
00:00:28,028 --> 00:00:29,362
- [TIRES SCREECH]
- [CAR HORN HONKS]

15
00:00:29,446 --> 00:00:31,114
- [CALOY GRUNTS]
<i>- Caloy!</i>

16
00:00:42,292 --> 00:00:43,585
[BILLY] <i>I knew it.</i>

17
00:00:46,254 --> 00:00:48,381
[MARIELA] <i>This is Abi.</i>

18
00:00:48,465 --> 00:00:49,966
<i>She's my eldest child.</i>

19
00:00:50,049 --> 00:00:52,010
<i>And this one here is Bea.</i>

20
00:00:52,093 --> 00:00:54,763
<i>She's the one who I thought</i>
<i>was working for you.</i>

21
00:00:54,846 --> 00:00:58,183
<i>- Perfect! Bea's on her way home.</i>
- [PHONE RINGING]

22
00:00:58,266 --> 00:01:02,896
[BILLY] <i>I also don't understand</i>
<i>why she has to use her sister's identity.</i>

23
00:01:03,646 --> 00:01:05,065
<i>Is she hiding from someone?</i>

24
00:01:05,148 --> 00:01:06,316
[KNOCKING ON DOOR]

25
00:01:07,859 --> 00:01:09,778
<i>Bea Dominguez.</i>

26
00:01:10,528 --> 00:01:12,572
<i>Could you come with us</i>
<i>to the police station?</i>

27
00:01:16,284 --> 00:01:18,828
- We've already used this one.
- Caloy and Abi are together.

28
00:01:18,912 --> 00:01:22,082
- Too predictable, no.
- Then Abi came here unannounced.

29
00:01:22,165 --> 00:01:23,875
This one looks good!
What do you guys think?

30
00:01:23,958 --> 00:01:26,127
She was spying on us.
I mean, even I don't understand--

31
00:01:26,211 --> 00:01:28,129
- Hello?
- Yes, chief?

32
00:01:28,213 --> 00:01:30,006
We need something stronger.

33
00:01:32,258 --> 00:01:34,135
Chief, I'm sorry. Give us a minute.

34
00:01:34,219 --> 00:01:36,971
We're so distracted by the other issue.

35
00:01:37,055 --> 00:01:40,517
I mean, it's wild. Abi is actually Bea?

36
00:01:40,600 --> 00:01:45,563
Plus, it's also possible that both she
and Caloy are criminals?!

37
00:01:45,647 --> 00:01:49,901
So basically, the puppet master
who's been manipulating Caloy

38
00:01:49,984 --> 00:01:51,277
is actually Abi?

39
00:01:51,361 --> 00:01:53,113
Or rather, Bea!

40
00:01:53,196 --> 00:01:55,073
- [MARJ] So wild!
- Mm-hmm.

41
00:01:55,156 --> 00:01:56,533
[VALERIE] Finally.

42
00:01:57,867 --> 00:01:59,536
Now you guys know!

43
00:02:00,954 --> 00:02:02,872
Oh, sorry…

44
00:02:03,623 --> 00:02:06,835
What we don't know right now
is what her motive is.

45
00:02:06,918 --> 00:02:11,089
This isn't simply because
I rejected her application.

46
00:02:11,172 --> 00:02:12,841
There's a deeper reason.

47
00:02:14,676 --> 00:02:15,844
But what could it be?

48
00:02:15,927 --> 00:02:17,887
[PENSIVE MUSIC PLAYING]

49
00:02:17,971 --> 00:02:21,099
- [CHATTERING INDISTINCTLY]
- [PHONE CHIMES]

50
00:02:23,268 --> 00:02:27,188
[PENSIVE MUSIC CONTINUES]

51
00:02:27,272 --> 00:02:29,983
Please keep working on this. I have to go.

52
00:02:30,066 --> 00:02:32,527
Sorry. Go, continue. Thank you!

53
00:02:35,572 --> 00:02:37,615
How do you know Carlos Toledo?

54
00:02:37,699 --> 00:02:40,201
How are you related him?

55
00:02:40,285 --> 00:02:43,872
[SUSPENSEFUL MUSIC PLAYING]

56
00:02:43,955 --> 00:02:46,541
Carlos Toledo?

57
00:02:46,624 --> 00:02:47,750
Who is that?

58
00:02:48,418 --> 00:02:50,336
I don't know him, ma'am.

59
00:02:50,420 --> 00:02:52,463
I don't have anything to do with him.

60
00:02:52,547 --> 00:02:54,090
Are you sure?

61
00:02:54,173 --> 00:03:00,597
[SUSPENSEFUL MUSIC CONTINUES]

62
00:03:11,566 --> 00:03:14,485
So Carlos was his name!

63
00:03:14,569 --> 00:03:15,904
Oh, ma'am…

64
00:03:16,404 --> 00:03:19,574
I just met him at a karaoke bar
and sang a duet with him.

65
00:03:19,657 --> 00:03:21,200
I don't know him at all!

66
00:03:21,284 --> 00:03:24,579
Is singing a duet considered a crime now?

67
00:03:25,371 --> 00:03:27,999
- No.
- There you go, ma'am!

68
00:03:28,082 --> 00:03:31,127
Then why am I still here? Can I leave now?

69
00:03:31,711 --> 00:03:36,174
We invited you here
because your name was mentioned

70
00:03:36,257 --> 00:03:38,551
in the statement given by Jordan Valentin.

71
00:03:39,969 --> 00:03:42,639
If you have no connection
to Carlos Toledo,

72
00:03:42,722 --> 00:03:48,228
why are his calls to you registered
on his cell phone?

73
00:03:48,311 --> 00:03:51,898
[SUSPENSEFUL MUSIC CONTINUES]

74
00:03:51,981 --> 00:03:53,858
- [THUDS]
- I knew it!

75
00:03:53,942 --> 00:03:58,321
He stole my phone that night!

76
00:03:58,404 --> 00:04:00,949
What a jerk! He was the one--

77
00:04:01,032 --> 00:04:03,660
He stole my phone, ma'am,
so I'm clueless about that.

78
00:04:03,743 --> 00:04:06,871
You know what? I don't know him at all.

79
00:04:06,955 --> 00:04:08,957
I also don't know
what you're talking about.

80
00:04:09,040 --> 00:04:11,793
Ma'am, please, I really need to go.

81
00:04:11,876 --> 00:04:14,128
I'm really late for work.

82
00:04:14,212 --> 00:04:16,005
I even dressed nice today!

83
00:04:16,089 --> 00:04:17,423
You can't leave yet.

84
00:04:18,049 --> 00:04:19,801
We still need to talk about

85
00:04:19,884 --> 00:04:24,389
why you're using your sister's identity.

86
00:04:24,472 --> 00:04:30,311
[SUSPENSEFUL MUSIC CONTINUES]

87
00:04:31,896 --> 00:04:38,611
[THEME MUSIC PLAYING]

88
00:05:16,149 --> 00:05:18,026
I just spoke to the attending physician.

89
00:05:19,193 --> 00:05:21,404
Caloy is still unconscious.

90
00:05:22,113 --> 00:05:25,033
Because of that,
we can't get a statement from him.

91
00:05:25,116 --> 00:05:28,077
But even without his testimony,

92
00:05:28,161 --> 00:05:30,747
we still have a strong case
against Bea Mercado.

93
00:05:33,374 --> 00:05:35,209
I just hope, now that she's cornered,

94
00:05:35,293 --> 00:05:37,045
she'll finally tell the truth.

95
00:05:37,962 --> 00:05:41,049
I don't understand
where her anger is coming from.

96
00:05:43,051 --> 00:05:44,302
By the way,

97
00:05:44,385 --> 00:05:46,721
we've prepared the restraining order
against your father.

98
00:05:46,804 --> 00:05:48,681
- Just in case.
- Wait a minute.

99
00:05:48,765 --> 00:05:50,349
He's still pestering you?

100
00:05:52,977 --> 00:05:55,063
Oh, thank you.

101
00:05:55,146 --> 00:05:58,733
You know, ever since you started working
here, I've felt a lot more at ease.

102
00:05:58,816 --> 00:06:00,568
Because even if Billy and I aren't here,

103
00:06:00,651 --> 00:06:03,571
someone's keeping an eye on our youngest.

104
00:06:03,654 --> 00:06:07,825
Oliver said you've also been
defending him from bullies.

105
00:06:07,909 --> 00:06:11,662
Honestly, Oliver can take them on.

106
00:06:11,746 --> 00:06:14,415
- He's a brave kid.
- Mm-hmm.

107
00:06:14,499 --> 00:06:16,459
He and Billy actually remind me
of my children.

108
00:06:16,542 --> 00:06:18,920
Oh? By the way, where are your kids?

109
00:06:19,921 --> 00:06:22,590
Ah… They're abroad.

110
00:06:23,299 --> 00:06:24,842
Are they the same age as Oliver?

111
00:06:26,594 --> 00:06:27,762
He's the same age as my youngest.

112
00:06:27,845 --> 00:06:32,058
Mm… Are they all abroad with your wife?

113
00:06:32,141 --> 00:06:34,060
[MOROSE MUSIC PLAYING]

114
00:06:34,143 --> 00:06:35,728
Um…

115
00:06:35,812 --> 00:06:37,146
I'm already widowed.

116
00:06:37,230 --> 00:06:38,981
If it weren't for my kids,

117
00:06:39,690 --> 00:06:41,651
I'd be alone in life.

118
00:06:42,235 --> 00:06:44,987
Same here. If it weren't
for Oliver and Billy,

119
00:06:45,071 --> 00:06:47,156
I'd be alone in life too.

120
00:06:47,824 --> 00:06:49,659
How did you end up living together anyway?

121
00:06:50,284 --> 00:06:54,455
Well, I used to work at
the social welfare department.

122
00:06:55,039 --> 00:06:58,626
We took the two of them under our custody

123
00:06:59,252 --> 00:07:02,880
after they became orphans
when Oliver was still a baby.

124
00:07:02,964 --> 00:07:05,299
We tried to look for
a foster home for them,

125
00:07:05,383 --> 00:07:07,426
but because of their age gap,

126
00:07:07,510 --> 00:07:09,762
there was a possibility that
they would be separated.

127
00:07:09,846 --> 00:07:11,973
Oh, Billy didn't like that.

128
00:07:12,056 --> 00:07:14,058
She was already a fighter at a young age,

129
00:07:14,142 --> 00:07:17,687
and she wouldn't allow anything
or anyone to separate them.

130
00:07:17,770 --> 00:07:21,399
In fact, she tried to run away
with Oliver many times.

131
00:07:22,024 --> 00:07:23,985
They lived in all sorts of places.

132
00:07:24,068 --> 00:07:25,987
On the street…

133
00:07:26,070 --> 00:07:28,448
Under the bridge…

134
00:07:28,531 --> 00:07:30,283
At a waiting shed…

135
00:07:30,366 --> 00:07:35,746
When I found them at a convenience store,
that's when I decided to adopt them.

136
00:07:35,830 --> 00:07:40,042
And that was the best decision
I've made in my life.

137
00:07:40,126 --> 00:07:44,338
To take care of them
and make them my family…

138
00:07:44,422 --> 00:07:47,300
To treat them like my own children.

139
00:07:47,383 --> 00:07:48,926
[PHONE CHIMES]

140
00:07:50,011 --> 00:07:52,054
Oh, excuse me.

141
00:07:53,055 --> 00:07:55,308
Sorry, but I have to go.

142
00:07:55,391 --> 00:07:56,350
Thank you, Sir Eric.

143
00:07:57,768 --> 00:07:58,978
Hey, thank you.

144
00:07:59,061 --> 00:08:00,605
For what?

145
00:08:02,064 --> 00:08:04,192
Nothing. Nothing.

146
00:08:04,275 --> 00:08:09,655
[MOROSE MUSIC CONTINUES]

147
00:08:09,739 --> 00:08:11,741
[MUSIC FADES]

148
00:08:11,824 --> 00:08:13,326
Ugh!

149
00:08:13,409 --> 00:08:14,827
Tsk!

150
00:08:14,911 --> 00:08:16,370
Sir?

151
00:08:16,454 --> 00:08:18,414
Ma'am?

152
00:08:18,498 --> 00:08:20,833
Can you let me go home now?

153
00:08:22,043 --> 00:08:24,504
You can't do this!

154
00:08:25,254 --> 00:08:27,548
This is illegal detention!

155
00:08:29,967 --> 00:08:31,594
Please!

156
00:08:32,678 --> 00:08:34,430
Ma'am? Sir?

157
00:08:35,223 --> 00:08:36,766
You don't have evidence!

158
00:08:36,849 --> 00:08:40,019
No evidence, no crime, right?

159
00:08:40,102 --> 00:08:41,771
And there's no evidence!

160
00:08:41,854 --> 00:08:43,356
- [BILLY GRUNTS]
- [LOUD THUD]

161
00:08:43,439 --> 00:08:45,942
The outpatient form
you left at Angels of Grace

162
00:08:46,025 --> 00:08:49,612
and the application form
you submitted to LoveList

163
00:08:49,695 --> 00:08:52,949
are both under the name Abigail Mercado.

164
00:08:53,699 --> 00:08:56,285
You didn't just fake your certificate.

165
00:08:57,745 --> 00:09:00,164
You forged the name. The address.

166
00:09:00,248 --> 00:09:01,624
The educational background.

167
00:09:01,707 --> 00:09:03,501
You faked everything.

168
00:09:05,586 --> 00:09:06,796
Bea.

169
00:09:06,879 --> 00:09:08,130
[TENSE MUSIC PLAYING]

170
00:09:08,214 --> 00:09:10,883
There are several cases
we can file against you.

171
00:09:10,967 --> 00:09:12,343
Identity theft.

172
00:09:12,426 --> 00:09:15,429
Falsification of documents.
Malicious mischief.

173
00:09:18,558 --> 00:09:19,767
Wait a minute.

174
00:09:20,560 --> 00:09:23,563
Even if I really used my sister's name,

175
00:09:23,646 --> 00:09:24,814
so what?

176
00:09:24,897 --> 00:09:27,024
Did I hurt anyone?

177
00:09:27,108 --> 00:09:29,569
Did I murder someone?

178
00:09:29,652 --> 00:09:31,737
You stole something.

179
00:09:31,821 --> 00:09:34,282
[STIRRING MUSIC PLAYING]

180
00:09:34,365 --> 00:09:36,867
How shallow, Ms. Billy Idol!

181
00:09:36,951 --> 00:09:40,538
That was just an idea!
Anyone could've thought of that idea!

182
00:09:40,621 --> 00:09:43,249
[BEA] Because everyone has a brain.

183
00:09:43,332 --> 00:09:45,376
Save your energy, Bea.

184
00:09:45,459 --> 00:09:47,628
[BILLY] You still have a lot
of cases to deal with.

185
00:09:48,254 --> 00:09:49,964
Your relationship with Caloy?

186
00:09:51,090 --> 00:09:53,175
I believe that's counted as conspiracy.

187
00:09:53,259 --> 00:09:55,261
[STIRRING MUSIC CONTINUES]

188
00:09:55,344 --> 00:09:56,971
You're no better. Relationship?

189
00:09:57,054 --> 00:09:58,681
Who is that man? I don't even know him.

190
00:09:58,764 --> 00:10:00,933
We don't have a relationship.

191
00:10:01,017 --> 00:10:02,268
You don't?

192
00:10:02,351 --> 00:10:03,561
[BEA] We don't!

193
00:10:04,812 --> 00:10:06,105
So what is this?

194
00:10:10,318 --> 00:10:17,325
[STIRRING MUSIC CONTINUES]

195
00:10:17,950 --> 00:10:19,660
For once, Bea,

196
00:10:19,744 --> 00:10:21,078
tell the truth.

197
00:10:26,000 --> 00:10:27,752
What did I ever do to you?

198
00:10:27,835 --> 00:10:33,716
[TENSE MUSIC PLAYING]

199
00:10:36,135 --> 00:10:37,386
Answer me!

200
00:10:41,807 --> 00:10:45,269
I don't need to explain anything
to you, Ms. Billy.

201
00:10:47,438 --> 00:10:48,856
[BILLY SCOFFS]

202
00:10:48,939 --> 00:10:50,858
[TENSE MUSIC CONTINUES]

203
00:10:50,941 --> 00:10:52,985
[GRANADO] We have evidence

204
00:10:53,069 --> 00:10:56,864
showing that you unlawfully
obtained confidential files

205
00:10:56,947 --> 00:10:58,324
from Ms. Cariño's company,

206
00:10:58,407 --> 00:11:01,827
and subsequently used it
for your personal gain.

207
00:11:01,911 --> 00:11:03,871
[GRANADO] That constitutes what?

208
00:11:03,954 --> 00:11:07,583
Copyright infringement
and qualified theft.

209
00:11:08,751 --> 00:11:11,170
Attorney, you're saying
so much about evidence,

210
00:11:11,253 --> 00:11:12,338
but you've shown me nothing.

211
00:11:12,421 --> 00:11:14,298
Show me the evidence first!

212
00:11:14,965 --> 00:11:16,634
[BEA] I'll get going then.

213
00:11:16,717 --> 00:11:18,344
I still have work to do.

214
00:11:18,427 --> 00:11:19,887
You're disturbing me.

215
00:11:19,970 --> 00:11:21,055
[TENSE MUSIC CONTINUES]

216
00:11:21,138 --> 00:11:23,933
[POLICE OFFICER] You can't go yet, ma'am.
Your questioning isn't over yet.

217
00:11:24,016 --> 00:11:26,685
It's not over yet, sir?
I've been here for so long!

218
00:11:26,769 --> 00:11:29,230
They asked a lot of questions,
and I answered them all!

219
00:11:29,939 --> 00:11:31,107
[BEA SCOFFS]

220
00:11:31,941 --> 00:11:33,526
What are you doing? Move over!

221
00:11:33,609 --> 00:11:36,153
- That's a violation, ma'am.
- What violation?! [GRUNTS]

222
00:11:36,237 --> 00:11:38,531
- Resistance and disobedience, ma'am!
- [BEA SCOFFS]

223
00:11:38,614 --> 00:11:40,950
Wait, you can't do that!
I can't get jailed!

224
00:11:41,033 --> 00:11:42,743
- [BEA GRUNTS]
- Stop moving.

225
00:11:42,827 --> 00:11:45,121
[BEA] You won't put me behind bars, right?

226
00:11:45,204 --> 00:11:46,789
- What are you doing?
- [CUFFS CLICKING]

227
00:11:49,750 --> 00:11:51,877
It's already happening, Bea.

228
00:11:51,961 --> 00:11:58,259
[TENSE MUSIC CONTINUES]

229
00:12:02,096 --> 00:12:05,057
This is our thank-you gift
from Angels of Grace.

230
00:12:06,976 --> 00:12:08,561
Oh, thank you.

231
00:12:08,644 --> 00:12:10,146
[PRECIOUS GIGGLES SOFTLY]

232
00:12:10,229 --> 00:12:11,564
Wow.

233
00:12:13,065 --> 00:12:14,024
A notebook?

234
00:12:14,108 --> 00:12:15,443
Mm-hmm.

235
00:12:15,526 --> 00:12:16,610
You know,

236
00:12:17,319 --> 00:12:20,489
I'm going to write
our memories together here.

237
00:12:20,573 --> 00:12:23,325
You're such an expert sweet-talker.

238
00:12:24,118 --> 00:12:25,828
I'm serious, Precious.

239
00:12:27,246 --> 00:12:28,414
You know,

240
00:12:29,290 --> 00:12:32,710
I know you're happy
when you're with Billy and Oliver.

241
00:12:33,335 --> 00:12:34,420
But

242
00:12:35,004 --> 00:12:36,881
keep in mind that one day,

243
00:12:37,590 --> 00:12:39,133
they will build their own families,

244
00:12:39,216 --> 00:12:40,676
and they will move out.

245
00:12:41,635 --> 00:12:42,928
So

246
00:12:43,012 --> 00:12:44,930
if you were to accept me,

247
00:12:45,014 --> 00:12:47,016
I would like to apply as…

248
00:12:47,099 --> 00:12:49,518
[CHUCKLES] My caregiver?

249
00:12:50,561 --> 00:12:52,688
Forever companion!

250
00:12:52,771 --> 00:12:55,858
[SOFT MUSIC PLAYING]

251
00:12:55,941 --> 00:12:59,236
Who would ever want
to grow old alone, right?

252
00:12:59,320 --> 00:13:03,240
But I need to think first
before making such a decision.

253
00:13:03,324 --> 00:13:05,367
Trusting someone

254
00:13:06,452 --> 00:13:08,412
is not that simple.

255
00:13:09,580 --> 00:13:12,291
[SOFT MUSIC CONTINUES]

256
00:13:12,374 --> 00:13:14,168
Willing to wait, ma'am.

257
00:13:15,336 --> 00:13:17,004
But just don't make me wait forever.

258
00:13:17,087 --> 00:13:18,881
[BRANDON CHUCKLES]

259
00:13:19,507 --> 00:13:20,758
Thank you.

260
00:13:23,135 --> 00:13:27,181
Giving that woman a chance
was really a huge mistake.

261
00:13:27,264 --> 00:13:28,349
Mm…

262
00:13:28,432 --> 00:13:30,476
She's already in jail, isn't she?

263
00:13:31,352 --> 00:13:34,230
But I still have a lot of questions
in my mind, Aunt Pres.

264
00:13:34,313 --> 00:13:35,397
Why?

265
00:13:36,190 --> 00:13:37,650
Why me?

266
00:13:37,733 --> 00:13:39,276
Dear, what matters is that

267
00:13:39,360 --> 00:13:44,323
Bea won't be able to make another move
against the company or against you.

268
00:13:44,406 --> 00:13:46,408
Well, she finally met her match.

269
00:13:46,492 --> 00:13:49,495
This woman's got some guts, doesn't she?

270
00:13:49,578 --> 00:13:51,997
You know the truth, Auntie Pres?

271
00:13:52,081 --> 00:13:53,832
I'm scared too.

272
00:13:53,916 --> 00:13:56,210
I'm just acting brave because I have to.

273
00:13:56,293 --> 00:14:01,590
[MOROSE MUSIC PLAYING]

274
00:14:01,674 --> 00:14:03,676
- Billy!
- Hmm?

275
00:14:03,759 --> 00:14:06,387
Look! I got a perfect score
on my science exam.

276
00:14:06,470 --> 00:14:08,180
One hundred out of one hundred!

277
00:14:08,764 --> 00:14:10,015
Hmm.

278
00:14:12,810 --> 00:14:13,936
[OLIVER] What is it?

279
00:14:14,687 --> 00:14:17,231
Looks like you're going to be
getting first honors again.

280
00:14:17,982 --> 00:14:19,608
I'm getting tired.

281
00:14:20,109 --> 00:14:20,943
Huh?

282
00:14:24,655 --> 00:14:26,991
I'm getting tired of going up on stage

283
00:14:27,074 --> 00:14:29,368
just to hang your medal,
you little rascal!

284
00:14:29,451 --> 00:14:30,578
Practice, practice!

285
00:14:30,661 --> 00:14:31,620
- Practice!
- Okay.

286
00:14:31,704 --> 00:14:33,956
And our first honor is

287
00:14:34,039 --> 00:14:35,708
Oliver Cariño!

288
00:14:35,791 --> 00:14:37,710
Whoo!

289
00:14:37,793 --> 00:14:39,628
- Thank you, thank you.
- Let me put this on you.

290
00:14:39,712 --> 00:14:41,797
Congratulations!

291
00:14:41,881 --> 00:14:43,382
Very good!

292
00:14:43,465 --> 00:14:46,010
Wow, this really makes
all the hard work worth it.

293
00:14:46,093 --> 00:14:47,761
Very good, my baby boy!

294
00:14:47,845 --> 00:14:50,306
- I'm not a baby boy anymore.
- Oh, you're a big boy now.

295
00:14:50,389 --> 00:14:53,058
Very good, my big boy!

296
00:14:53,142 --> 00:14:54,184
[SQUEALING]

297
00:14:56,186 --> 00:14:59,481
Ma, I won't be able
to come home tonight, okay?

298
00:14:59,565 --> 00:15:01,317
What do you mean you won't?

299
00:15:01,400 --> 00:15:02,610
Why?

300
00:15:03,402 --> 00:15:04,486
Uh…

301
00:15:04,570 --> 00:15:07,531
I still have some things to take care of
here at the station.

302
00:15:07,615 --> 00:15:08,699
There's still a lot to do.

303
00:15:09,199 --> 00:15:10,868
What do you need to do?

304
00:15:10,951 --> 00:15:13,037
Why? Are you going to jail?

305
00:15:13,621 --> 00:15:15,623
No. I'm not.

306
00:15:15,706 --> 00:15:17,166
I'm coming over there.

307
00:15:17,249 --> 00:15:18,250
<i>Ma, don't!</i>

308
00:15:18,334 --> 00:15:19,543
Please don't come.

309
00:15:19,627 --> 00:15:21,462
I'm okay. I promise.

310
00:15:21,545 --> 00:15:23,756
What happened?

311
00:15:25,299 --> 00:15:27,217
Don't worry about me, Ma.

312
00:15:27,301 --> 00:15:29,094
I'm okay, all right?

313
00:15:29,637 --> 00:15:31,305
Go get some sleep.

314
00:15:31,388 --> 00:15:34,600
This is Billy's doing, isn't it?

315
00:15:34,683 --> 00:15:37,019
She's the one framing you, right?

316
00:15:37,853 --> 00:15:38,854
Ma.

317
00:15:38,938 --> 00:15:41,774
Ma, listen to me.

318
00:15:42,441 --> 00:15:43,943
<i>Ma, I'm okay.</i>

319
00:15:44,652 --> 00:15:46,654
<i>Just leave Billy alone.</i>

320
00:15:46,737 --> 00:15:48,113
<i>Don't think about her.</i>

321
00:15:48,906 --> 00:15:50,699
If she wants a fight,

322
00:15:51,909 --> 00:15:53,994
I'll give her one.

323
00:15:54,078 --> 00:15:56,747
[OMINOUS MUSIC PLAYING]

324
00:15:56,830 --> 00:15:57,957
[BIRDS CHIRPING]

325
00:15:58,540 --> 00:16:02,795
Attorney, why was Bea suddenly released?

326
00:16:02,878 --> 00:16:04,630
Bea was released on bail.

327
00:16:04,713 --> 00:16:08,175
But that doesn't mean the cases
against her won't move forward.

328
00:16:08,258 --> 00:16:11,428
<i>If she thinks she's</i>
<i>off the hook, she's wrong.</i>

329
00:16:11,512 --> 00:16:14,056
<i>We're just waiting</i>
<i>for the prosecutor's resolution.</i>

330
00:16:14,139 --> 00:16:16,183
<i>Once it's filed in court</i>

331
00:16:16,266 --> 00:16:18,227
<i>and probable cause is found,</i>

332
00:16:18,310 --> 00:16:21,021
<i>the court can issue</i>
<i>a warrant for her arrest.</i>

333
00:16:21,105 --> 00:16:25,818
But remember, the charges we filed
against her are bailable.

334
00:16:25,901 --> 00:16:28,612
So she can still be released
while the case is ongoing.

335
00:16:29,405 --> 00:16:33,367
The only way to keep her in jail
is to get that conviction.

336
00:16:33,450 --> 00:16:35,494
Then we'll secure a conviction

337
00:16:35,577 --> 00:16:37,413
so Bea ends up behind bars for good.

338
00:16:37,997 --> 00:16:40,874
Attorney, Carlos Toledo is the key.

339
00:16:41,458 --> 00:16:42,918
If we can get Caloy to confess,

340
00:16:43,002 --> 00:16:45,546
Bea will definitely be implicated.

341
00:16:45,629 --> 00:16:48,716
According to his doctor, he's stable now,
but he's still unconscious.

342
00:16:48,799 --> 00:16:51,010
He could wake up at any time.

343
00:16:51,093 --> 00:16:54,596
[TENSE MUSIC PLAYING]

344
00:16:54,680 --> 00:16:56,432
Can I have five minutes alone?

345
00:16:57,141 --> 00:16:58,684
- Okay.
- Thank you.

346
00:17:03,272 --> 00:17:04,106
Caloy?

347
00:17:05,357 --> 00:17:06,233
Wake up.

348
00:17:09,820 --> 00:17:10,946
[CALOY GRUNTS]

349
00:17:11,030 --> 00:17:13,949
[TENSE MUSIC CONTINUES]

350
00:17:14,992 --> 00:17:15,993
I knew it.

351
00:17:17,119 --> 00:17:18,579
You're just pretending.

352
00:17:18,662 --> 00:17:20,122
[GRUNTS IN PAIN]

353
00:17:20,205 --> 00:17:23,834
Caloy, we already know
Bea Mercado's the one giving you orders.

354
00:17:23,917 --> 00:17:26,128
Why does she want to destroy Billy?

355
00:17:26,211 --> 00:17:28,338
- I don't know! I don't know anything!
- Talk!

356
00:17:28,422 --> 00:17:30,049
- Talk!
- [CALOY GRUNTING]

357
00:17:30,132 --> 00:17:31,341
- Talk!
- Ow!

358
00:17:31,884 --> 00:17:33,844
- Talk!
- Ow!

359
00:17:33,927 --> 00:17:34,970
- Help!
- Caloy!

360
00:17:35,054 --> 00:17:37,181
- I can do this all day!
- Sir, what are you doing?

361
00:17:37,264 --> 00:17:38,682
- Help!
- Sir, let him go!

362
00:17:38,766 --> 00:17:40,017
It hurts! [GRUNTS]

363
00:17:46,940 --> 00:17:51,070
[JORDAN] So Caloy is
threatening to press charges?

364
00:17:52,488 --> 00:17:53,697
What did you expect?

365
00:17:53,781 --> 00:17:56,325
Of course he wouldn't confess.
You attacked him.

366
00:17:56,408 --> 00:17:58,410
How else was I supposed
to know he was lying?

367
00:17:58,494 --> 00:17:59,745
And he was.

368
00:17:59,828 --> 00:18:01,830
But I still got nothing from him.

369
00:18:01,914 --> 00:18:04,249
[GLOOMY MUSIC PLAYING]

370
00:18:04,333 --> 00:18:08,378
Abi, as expected,
made her way back to Pebblng.

371
00:18:09,088 --> 00:18:10,214
How?

372
00:18:10,297 --> 00:18:12,007
Camille helped.

373
00:18:12,091 --> 00:18:13,217
How do you know?

374
00:18:13,300 --> 00:18:16,095
[DRAMATIC MUSIC SWELLS]

375
00:18:23,811 --> 00:18:26,980
[TENSE MUSIC PLAYING]

376
00:18:27,064 --> 00:18:28,982
Boss Zandro sent me.

377
00:18:29,066 --> 00:18:30,400
He wanted to remind you

378
00:18:30,984 --> 00:18:34,113
that no one has ever outsmarted him,
especially when it comes to money.

379
00:18:34,780 --> 00:18:36,615
I already told him.

380
00:18:37,366 --> 00:18:39,701
I just need a little time.

381
00:18:39,785 --> 00:18:41,245
I'll find a way to pay him back.

382
00:18:41,829 --> 00:18:43,372
You better make sure of it.

383
00:18:44,081 --> 00:18:45,958
I'll give you ten days.

384
00:18:46,875 --> 00:18:48,710
After that, I'll collect the debt myself.

385
00:18:48,794 --> 00:18:50,546
[TENSE MUSIC CONTINUES]

386
00:18:50,629 --> 00:18:52,422
Do I make myself clear?

387
00:18:55,676 --> 00:19:00,013
[TENSE MUSIC CONTINUES]

388
00:19:08,147 --> 00:19:09,189
[MORRIE] Coffee.

389
00:19:09,731 --> 00:19:10,649
Uh…

390
00:19:11,608 --> 00:19:12,985
Thank you, Morrie.

391
00:19:13,068 --> 00:19:14,361
Are you okay?

392
00:19:14,862 --> 00:19:17,948
I can't imagine being in your situation.

393
00:19:18,031 --> 00:19:19,867
You went to jail for what?

394
00:19:19,950 --> 00:19:21,493
Two, three days?

395
00:19:23,745 --> 00:19:26,582
But the allegations
against me aren't true.

396
00:19:27,624 --> 00:19:29,877
Good thing Ms. Camille helped me.

397
00:19:30,544 --> 00:19:34,548
What matters to me
is that she believed me.

398
00:19:35,883 --> 00:19:37,009
Okay.

399
00:19:37,092 --> 00:19:38,760
Well, I'm glad you're back.

400
00:19:38,844 --> 00:19:40,637
We really took a hit while you were gone.

401
00:19:40,721 --> 00:19:41,722
Oh?

402
00:19:44,808 --> 00:19:46,435
Okay, how's it going?

403
00:19:48,187 --> 00:19:49,062
Um…

404
00:19:49,730 --> 00:19:51,481
I'm almost done, Ms. Camille.

405
00:19:51,565 --> 00:19:54,610
The ad banners have also
been activated in our app.

406
00:19:54,693 --> 00:19:56,945
We're all set for next week.

407
00:19:57,029 --> 00:19:59,615
I knew it wasn't a mistake
to give you another chance.

408
00:19:59,698 --> 00:20:02,075
[STIRRING MUSIC PLAYING]

409
00:20:02,159 --> 00:20:03,452
Ms. Camille,

410
00:20:04,411 --> 00:20:06,622
thank you again

411
00:20:06,705 --> 00:20:09,958
for giving me a chance.

412
00:20:10,042 --> 00:20:15,505
I only used my sister's name
because of her credentials.

413
00:20:15,589 --> 00:20:18,800
Because who would hire someone

414
00:20:18,884 --> 00:20:22,387
who's just an internet cafe owner
with a college degree,

415
00:20:22,471 --> 00:20:25,015
but no honors or a master's degree?

416
00:20:25,098 --> 00:20:28,268
You had every reason not to hire me.

417
00:20:28,352 --> 00:20:30,020
Stop explaining.

418
00:20:30,103 --> 00:20:32,397
What I need from you
is for you to deliver.

419
00:20:32,481 --> 00:20:36,318
And that's what you've been doing
since you joined my company.

420
00:20:36,401 --> 00:20:39,363
You gave us LoveFeast,
and you've pulled in investors.

421
00:20:40,155 --> 00:20:42,699
So as much as you want to thank me,

422
00:20:42,783 --> 00:20:44,243
thank you.

423
00:20:44,326 --> 00:20:47,996
[STIRRING MUSIC CONTINUES]

424
00:20:48,080 --> 00:20:49,748
Thank you, Ms. Camille.

425
00:20:49,831 --> 00:20:55,337
[STIRRING MUSIC CONTINUES]

426
00:20:59,883 --> 00:21:02,427
[BILLY] <i>Our pilot project</i>
<i>for Happily Ever After.</i>

427
00:21:02,511 --> 00:21:04,596
<i>And our first couple, Melissa and Theo.</i>

428
00:21:04,680 --> 00:21:06,807
<i>Her dad does not approve of Theo.</i>

429
00:21:06,890 --> 00:21:08,183
<i>The bride doesn't seem to be happy.</i>

430
00:21:08,267 --> 00:21:10,894
<i>It won't be complete.</i>
<i>Not without my dad.</i>

431
00:21:10,978 --> 00:21:13,230
<i>Each fairytale has its own plot twist.</i>

432
00:21:13,313 --> 00:21:15,565
<i>Your job's simple, so do it.</i>

433
00:21:15,649 --> 00:21:18,193
<i>Why are they on their phones?</i>
<i>They'll ruin the coverage.</i>

434
00:21:18,277 --> 00:21:19,569
<i>LoveList has an event.</i>

435
00:21:19,653 --> 00:21:21,571
<i>- At the same time as ours?</i>
<i>- Make love happen.</i>

436
00:21:21,655 --> 00:21:24,366
<i>Which one of us is the bigger thief?</i>

437
00:21:24,449 --> 00:21:26,451
<i>What's your reason for going after me?</i>

438
00:21:26,535 --> 00:21:29,955
[DOCTOR] <i>Mr. Toledo may now be</i>
<i>transferred into your custody.</i>

439
00:21:30,747 --> 00:21:32,749
- [BLOWS LAND]
- [GRUNTS, GROANS]

440
00:21:32,833 --> 00:21:35,961
<i>Caloy has to be caught.</i>
<i>Before they do anything else.</i>

441
00:21:38,797 --> 00:21:40,924
[BILLY] <i>We've always celebrated</i>
<i>our birthdays together.</i>

442
00:21:41,008 --> 00:21:42,426
<i>So it can't be just about me.</i>

443
00:21:42,509 --> 00:21:43,427
<i>I have another wish.</i>

444
00:21:43,510 --> 00:21:46,096
<i>Happiness for the people</i>
<i>I care about the most.</i>

445
00:21:46,179 --> 00:21:50,058
[SINGING] ♪ <i>Just lean on me ♪</i>

446
00:21:50,142 --> 00:21:53,270
[BEA] <i>I don't think it would hurt</i>
<i>to give her a proper scare.</i>

447
00:21:53,812 --> 00:21:55,439
- [BILLY SCREAMS]
<i>- Stop resisting!</i>

448
00:21:55,522 --> 00:21:57,649
<i>- Help! Let me go!</i>
<i>- Stop resisting!</i>

449
00:21:57,733 --> 00:21:59,067
- [BOTH GRUNT]
- [THUD]
